## 🛑 3. POPIA Consent Withdrawal Handler (Production-Ready)
*Handles user requests to withdraw consent per POPIA §11(3). Stops marketing, flags account, and updates FluentCRM instantly.*

### 🔹 Step 1: The PHP Handler (`functions-enhanced.php`)
```php
<?php
/**
 * POPIA Consent Withdrawal Handler
 * Allows users to revoke data processing consent via a secure link.
 * Compliant with POPIA §11(3) and §24 (Data Subject Rights).
 */

add_action('init', 'ngt_handle_popia_withdrawal');
function ngt_handle_popia_withdrawal() {
    // 1. Verify Nonce and Action
    if (!isset($_GET['ngt_withdraw_popia']) || !wp_verify_nonce($_GET['_wpnonce'], 'withdraw_popia')) {
        return;
    }

    $user_id = get_current_user_id();
    if (!$user_id) {
        wp_redirect(home_url('/login?redirect=' . urlencode($_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'])));
        exit;
    }

    // 2. Update WordPress Meta (Audit Trail)
    $withdrawal_log = [
        'given' => false,
        'withdrawn_at' => current_time('mysql'),
        'withdrawn_ip' => WC_Geolocation::get_ip_address(),
        'method' => 'dashboard_link'
    ];
    update_user_meta($user_id, '_ngt_popia_consent', $withdrawal_log);

    // 3. Update FluentCRM (Stop Marketing)
    if (class_exists('FluentCRM\App\Models\Contact')) {
        $contact = \FluentCRM\App\Models\Contact::where('user_id', $user_id)->first();
        if ($contact) {
            // Remove from all marketing lists
            $all_lists = \FluentCRM\App\Models\ContactList::all()->pluck('id')->toArray();
            $contact->detachLists($all_lists);

            // Add "Do Not Market" tag
            $tag = \FluentCRM\App\Models\ContactTag::firstOrCreate(['title' => 'POPIA Withdrawn']);
            $contact->attachTags([$tag->id]);

            // Update custom fields
            $contact->custom_fields['cf_popia_consent_given'] = false;
            $contact->custom_fields['cf_popia_withdrawal_date'] = current_time('mysql');
            $contact->save();
        }
    }

    // 4. Redirect with Success Message
    wp_redirect(add_query_arg('popia_status', 'withdrawn', home_url('/dashboard/')));
    exit;
}

// 5. Admin Notice for Dashboard
add_action('admin_notices', 'ngt_popia_withdrawal_notice');
function ngt_popia_withdrawal_notice() {
    if (isset($_GET['popia_status']) && $_GET['popia_status'] === 'withdrawn') {
        echo '<div class="notice notice-success is-dismissible"><p>✅ Your consent has been withdrawn. You will no longer receive marketing communications.</p></div>';
    }
}
```

### 🔹 Step 2: The Withdrawal Link (Add to Dashboard/Footer)
```html
<a href="<?= esc_url(add_query_arg([
    'ngt_withdraw_popia' => '1', 
    '_wpnonce' => wp_create_nonce('withdraw_popia')
], home_url('/dashboard/'))) ?>" 
   style="color:#dc2626; text-decoration:underline; font-size:13px;">
   Withdraw POPIA Consent
</a>
```

### 🔹 Step 3: Automated "Right to be Forgotten" Cleanup (Cron)
*Optional: Automatically anonymize data after 30 days of withdrawal if requested.*
```php
add_action('ngt_anonymize_withdrawn_data', 'ngt_anonymize_user_data');
function ngt_anonymize_user_data() {
    $users = get_users(['meta_key' => '_ngt_popia_consent', 'meta_compare' => 'EXISTS']);
    foreach ($users as $user) {
        $consent = get_user_meta($user->ID, '_ngt_popia_consent', true);
        if (is_array($consent) && !$consent['given'] && strtotime($consent['withdrawn_at']) < strtotime('-30 days')) {
            // Anonymize PII
            wp_update_user(['ID' => $user->ID, 'user_email' => 'deleted_' . $user->ID . '@nextgentutors.co.za']);
            delete_user_meta($user->ID, '_ngt_popia_consent');
            error_log("[NGT-POPIA] Anonymized user {$user->ID} after 30-day withdrawal period.");
        }
    }
}
// Schedule this to run weekly via WP-Cron
if (!wp_next_scheduled('ngt_anonymize_withdrawn_data')) {
    wp_schedule_event(time(), 'weekly', 'ngt_anonymize_withdrawn_data');
}
```

