## 📦 3. Automated DirectAdmin Staging Deployment Script

### 📁 `scripts/deploy-staging.sh`
```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# AI_AGENT: DirectAdmin Shared Hosting Staging Deploy
# Usage: ./scripts/deploy-staging.sh [environment]
set -euo pipefail

ENV=${1:-staging}
STAGING_USER="your_da_user"
STAGING_HOST="your_da_host"
STAGING_DIR="/home/${STAGING_USER}/domains/staging.nextgentutors.co.za/public_html"
REMOTE_USER="${STAGING_USER}"
SSH_KEY="${HOME}/.ssh/da_staging_ed25519"

echo "🚀 Starting $ENV deployment..."
echo "📦 Syncing files (excluding cache/vendor)..."
rsync -avz --delete \
  --exclude='.git/' \
  --exclude='vendor/' \
  --exclude='node_modules/' \
  --exclude='wp-content/uploads/' \
  --exclude='.env' \
  ./ "${REMOTE_USER}@${STAGING_HOST}:${STAGING_DIR}/"

echo "🔐 Securing permissions (DirectAdmin safe)..."
ssh -i "$SSH_KEY" "${REMOTE_USER}@${STAGING_HOST}" bash << 'EOF'
  cd "${STAGING_DIR}"
  find wp-content/uploads -type d -exec chmod 755 {} \;
  find wp-content/uploads -type f -exec chmod 644 {} \;
  chmod 644 wp-config.php .htaccess
  chown -R ${STAGING_USER}:${STAGING_USER} wp-content/
EOF

echo "🧹 Flushing caches & verifying..."
ssh -i "$SSH_KEY" "${REMOTE_USER}@${STAGING_HOST}" bash << 'EOF'
  cd "${STAGING_DIR}"
  if command -v wp &>/dev/null; then
    wp cache flush --allow-root 2>/dev/null || true
    wp cron test --allow-root 2>/dev/null || true
  else
    echo "⚠️ WP-CLI not available. Triggering cron via curl..."
    curl -s "https://staging.nextgentutors.co.za/wp-cron.php?doing_wp_cron" >/dev/null
  fi

  STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" https://staging.nextgentutors.co.za)
  if [ "$STATUS" -eq 200 ]; then
    echo "✅ Deployment successful. HTTP $STATUS"
  else
    echo "❌ Health check failed. HTTP $STATUS"
    exit 1
  fi
EOF

echo "🎉 $ENV deployment complete."
```
> ✅ **AI Agent Note**: Make executable: `chmod +x scripts/deploy-staging.sh`. DirectAdmin shared hosting restricts `sudo`/`systemctl`. This script uses user-level `chmod`/`chown` and falls back to `curl` for WP-Cron if `wp-cli` is unavailable.

