## 📧 2. WP-CLI Bulk Email Trigger (Test Automation)
*Sends a specific FluentCRM email to a list of users for testing templates and deliverability. Safe for staging.*

```php
#!/usr/bin/env php
<?php
/**
 * NextGen Tutors — Bulk Email Test Trigger
 * Usage: wp eval-file test-email-blast.php --email_id=123 --list="Active Customers" --limit=5
 */

if (!defined('WP_CLI') || !WP_CLI) die("Run via WP-CLI.\n");

$email_id = \WP_CLI\Utils\get_flag_value(WP_CLI::get_arguments(), '--email_id');
$list_name = \WP_CLI\Utils\get_flag_value(WP_CLI::get_arguments(), '--list', 'Active Customers');
$limit = \WP_CLI\Utils\get_flag_value(WP_CLI::get_arguments(), '--limit', 5);

if (!$email_id) WP_CLI::error("❌ Please specify --email_id");

$list = \FluentCRM\App\Models\ContactList::where('title', $list_name)->first();
if (!$list) WP_CLI::error("❌ List '{$list_name}' not found.");

$contacts = \FluentCRM\App\Models\Contact::whereHas('lists', function($q) use ($list) {
    $q->where('contact_lists.list_id', $list->id);
})->limit($limit)->get();

if ($contacts->isEmpty()) WP_CLI::error("❌ No contacts found in list.");

WP_CLI::log("🚀 Sending Email ID {$email_id} to {$contacts->count()} contacts in '{$list_name}'...");
$progress = \WP_CLI\Utils\make_progress_bar('Sending', $contacts->count());

foreach ($contacts as $contact) {
    try {
        // Use FluentCRM's internal email sending mechanism
        $emailService = new \FluentCRM\App\Services\Email\EmailService();
        $emailService->sendEmail($email_id, [$contact->id], []);
        $progress->tick();
    } catch (\Exception $e) {
        WP_CLI::warning("⚠️ Failed for {$contact->email}: " . $e->getMessage());
    }
}

$progress->finish();
WP_CLI::success("\n✅ Bulk trigger complete. Check FluentCRM → Reports for delivery status.");
```

